{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/87071-random-lunar-speculation","id":87071,"title":"Random Lunar speculation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-08T16:31:34-08:00","id":87071,"title":"Random Lunar speculation","content":"A few days ago I was going over the &quot;what we know&quot; wiki and I came across two quotes about Lunars that struck me as rather interesting. The first mentioned Lunars still having change as a theme, but with an emphasis on change over time. The second quote mentioned that the loss of two of the Lunar Casts would be an significant part of their backstory.<br /> <br /> Taken together, these two quotes imply to me that the loss of the Casts for Lunars is a deliberate thing, either built directly in to the Exaltation itself as a kind of evolution/adaptation to their circumstances, or that the Lunars can deliberately pick and choose their Casts, and that the Lost Casts have simply fallen out of use thanks to their current war with the Sidereals and the Realm (or some other option that I haven't thought of).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 03-08-2014, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T16:53:58-08:00","id":87083,"title":"","content":"I find it interesting that they say they've lost <i>two</i> of the Lunar castes, implying that the Changing Moon (or 3rd ed equivalent) was one of the original five.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T16:58:45-08:00","id":87087,"title":"","content":"That's an interesting theory, to be sure, but I have difficulty imagining how it would work mechanically.<br /> <br /> If the Exaltation changes over time, what causes it to do that? Can the changes be directed by the Luna, or the Lunars themselves?<br /> <br /> If the Lunars choose their exaltation type, how do they choose, and what would enable them to make an informed choice? I would guess that most people in Creation can't tell the castes of Anathema apart before they've had the difference explained to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T17:24:10-08:00","id":87098,"title":"","content":"My guess is that they're going to go beyond the &quot;band-aid&quot; solution modeled in previous editions and attempt to portray the Lunars as actually having performed <i>reconstructive surgery </i>on their Exaltations, as previous editions claimed.<br /> <br /> No Wyld Taint, no Wyld-related Chimerism, no Wyld-related Lost Castes.<br /> <br /> After the Primordial War, the Lunar Exalted reinvented themselves to make a place for themselves in a world where Exalted and humanity ruled Creation. After the Usurpation, the Lunar Exalted reinvented themselves again, to survive and conquer a world where the Solar Exalted had vanished, the Terrestrials and Sidereals ruled, and the Lunars themselves were hunted like beasts.<br /> <br /> The devs have told us before that a First Age game would operate on a scale that vanilla Exalted is not designed to properly handle. They said the same thing was even more true of the Primordial War. Storytellers and players are free to explore those eras, but the game isn't optimized for them the way it is for the pre-Shogunate world. So the developers are never again going to waste time providing content for playing the preceding eras.<br /> <br /> That means the Lost Castes (both sets) are supposed to be just as big a &quot;white-space&quot; as the exact number and roster of Primordials and Death Lords. You're free to make it up yourself, but it doesn't work for the game as a whole to nail that down.<br /> <br /> Whereas the first two editions bemoaned the loss of the Lost Castes and suggested recovering them as a worthy (if not required) pursuit for Lunar players wanting to &quot;win the game&quot;, I feel the third edition will say, &quot;&quot;You don't <i>need</i> the old Castes. These new Castes are <i>rad</i>, and you shouldn't take anyone pining for the old ones seriously.&quot;<br /> <br /> More, I feel the next edition will reverse the old ball-and-chain into a new and better challenge, &quot;If your current Castes aren't working for you any more, why try to recreate the failed past? <i>Make your own Castes</i>, to fit <i>your needs</i>. Do <i>better </i>than the old guys!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T17:40:57-08:00","id":87106,"title":"","content":"Sooooo what's the news?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T19:49:02-08:00","id":87164,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I like the idea of an Exalt being able to hack their Exaltation. It feels like it undermines the idea that Exaltation is &quot;divine fire gifted from the gods to mankind&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T19:56:52-08:00","id":87168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/87071-random-lunar-speculation?p=87164#post87164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I like the idea of an Exalt being able to hack their Exaltation. It feels like it undermines the idea that Exaltation is &quot;divine fire gifted from the gods to mankind&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just how Lunars roll. <br /> <br /> Lunars deliberately breaking their Castes would probably work best if their First Age Castes are all completely different from their Second Age Castes. Or if they're never described, which seems more likely. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T21:08:07-08:00","id":87198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/87071-random-lunar-speculation?p=87164#post87164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I like the idea of an Exalt being able to hack their Exaltation. It feels like it undermines the idea that Exaltation is &quot;divine fire gifted from the gods to mankind&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/87071-random-lunar-speculation?p=87168#post87168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just how Lunars roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Remember, we're not just talking about <i>any </i>Exalted modifying their Exaltations here. We're talking about the Chosen of the goddess with the power to define who and what she is in ways no others are. It seems plausible the particular divine fire she gifted to mankind can be modified by its recipients.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars deliberately breaking their Castes would probably work best if their First Age Castes are all completely different from their Second Age Castes. Or if they're never described, which seems more likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>At Aggiecon, Holden remarked that the Lunars of the Second Age have no need of a courtesan Caste. That said, I'd probably take it as more of an illustrative example, not necessarily something they had. I think you're right that we neither need nor are likely to get details on what the Castes used to be.<br /> <br /> Also, there's another little interesting tidbit from the same M\u00f8rke quote that the OP first alluded to:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beyond that, there is still a theme of &quot;change&quot; to them, but it is more about change-over-time, rather than a theme that changes every time you turn a page. In the Primordial War they were one thing, in the First Age, something else. When the First Age fell, they went through some major changes, that set them on the road to becoming what they are now. And I foresee a major change in their future\u2014one that sets the tone for their premise in EX3.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Castes are (a part) of what John means in there, that &quot;major change in their future&quot; suggests that Lunars becoming something other than they are now is very much in the cards.<br /> <br /> ... Heh. Depending on how flexible Lunar Exaltation hacking can be, it just struck me as a very clever thing the EX3 Team is doing. Ask a dozen forumites what they want Lunars to be, and you'll get at least as many answers. So they're telling us, &quot;Lunars are this,&quot; because of their response to their circumstances. But now there are new circumstances. In response to which Lunars can become whatever favored interpretation one has for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T21:16:50-08:00","id":87204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/87071-random-lunar-speculation?p=87198#post87198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Heh. Depending on how flexible Lunar Exaltation hacking can be, it just struck me as a very clever thing the EX3 Team is doing. Ask a dozen forumites what they want Lunars to be, and you'll get at least as many answers. So they're telling us, &quot;Lunars are this,&quot; because of their response to their circumstances. But now there are new circumstances. In response to which Lunars can become whatever favored interpretation one has for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they still probably won't be like TAW or produce exact duplicates of Mystique, I'm guessing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T21:37:22-08:00","id":87217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/87071-random-lunar-speculation?p=87204#post87204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they still probably won't be like TAW or produce exact duplicates of Mystique, I'm guessing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on how EX3 Lunars are written, but I'm not sure how much value there would be in nailing that down. If the important thing is that what Lunars were, are, and can be are not all the same, and there are reasons not to specify the former and the latter... why <i>not</i> leave it kind of open-ended?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T22:27:30-08:00","id":87240,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how anyone other than the Devs can make claims on &quot;that's how Lunars roll&quot;, when it seems like they're more or less getting rebuilt from the ground up. That said, I am very interested in seeing how they solve the Caste transition issue, although I stand by my assertion that &quot;hacking the exaltation&quot; would be a bad/dumb way to go about doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T22:32:06-08:00","id":87245,"title":"","content":"Well, since Neverborn and Yozi can do it, I see no reason Lunars can't do it too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T23:00:00-08:00","id":87267,"title":"","content":"True. I largely reject the notion that Exaltations are hackable because it goes against the idea that the devs seemed to be pushing that Exaltations are &quot;abstract, unquantifiable miracles&quot;. The yozi and the neverborn can get away with it because they're also being pushed in to the background as &quot;abstract, unquantifiable monstrosities&quot;. If this is no longer the case, then I withdraw my objections. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T23:04:27-08:00","id":87269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/87071-random-lunar-speculation?p=87267#post87267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. I largely reject the notion that Exaltations are hackable because it goes against the idea that the devs seemed to be pushing that Exaltations are &quot;abstract, unquantifiable miracles&quot;. The yozi and the neverborn can get away with it because they're also being pushed in to the background as &quot;abstract, unquantifiable monstrosities&quot;. If this is no longer the case, then I withdraw my objections. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It may still be that way, but Luna is very abstract too. She came from bloody Oramus. Some of that abstraction may rub off on her Chosen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T23:18:34-08:00","id":87279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/87071-random-lunar-speculation?p=87269#post87269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It may still be that way, but Luna is very abstract too. She came from bloody Oramus. Some of that abstraction may rub off on her Chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tell certainly did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T16:42:24-07:00","id":87802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/87071-random-lunar-speculation?p=87198#post87198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At Aggiecon, Holden remarked that the Lunars of the Second Age have no need of a <b>courtesan</b> Caste. That said, I'd probably take it as more of an illustrative example, not necessarily something they had. I think you're right that we neither need nor are likely to get details on what the Castes used to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'm hoping that <i>no </i>splat in 3E will have, have had, or eventually have need of a courtesan Caste because that just sounds like it'd make for reeeeeally awkward moments in play. :V<br /> <br /> ...seriously though, I'll be happy if 3E Lunars have rules for reinventing their roles - maybe the Exigents hardback will double as a modkit for other splats, and Lunars will just have a defined in-game means of breaking into that particular designspace?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}